<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Launch Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Product launches can become difficult when teams work without a
                    shared plan, responsibilities are unclear, or important readiness
                    activities are completed too late. Effective launch management
                    identifies these risks early and establishes clear processes
                    for addressing them.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Responsibilities:</b> When multiple teams are involved,
                    unclear ownership can result in missed activities and delays.
                    Clearly assigning responsibilities helps maintain accountability.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Incomplete Product Readiness:</b> Technical completion does not
                    always mean the product is ready for customers. Testing,
                    documentation, support, monitoring, and operational preparation
                    should also be completed.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Launch Delays:</b> Dependencies between engineering, marketing,
                    sales, and support can create delays. A detailed launch timeline
                    helps teams identify dependencies early.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Poor Internal Communication:</b> Teams may use inconsistent
                    messaging or miss important updates when communication is not
                    coordinated. A clear communication structure helps maintain
                    alignment.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Insufficient Customer Support:</b> Increased customer activity
                    after launch can generate additional questions and support requests.
                    Preparing support teams and resources before launch reduces this risk.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unexpected Technical Issues:</b> New products can experience
                    unexpected problems after release. Monitoring, incident processes,
                    rollback plans, and escalation procedures help teams respond quickly.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Limited Post-Launch Analysis:</b> Organizations may miss valuable
                    learnings when launch performance is not reviewed systematically.
                    A post-launch review helps improve future releases.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant launch challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

